  "summary": "The audit checks the 90 graduate units, at least 80 of them at the GSB, and the first-year core: the four Leadership Foundations courses, one course in each of the five Analytic Foundations areas, and at least 15 units of Management Foundations from three of the five categories. Core courses must be passed with LP or better on the grading basis the GSB sets; the audit does not read GSB grades, so check that yourself, along with the 70 letter-graded GSB units, the 80 letter-graded units (no more than 10 pass/fail), the 2.65 GSB GPA, the Global Experience and the Engaging with Differences Requirement by the start of winter quarter of the second year, and six quarters of full-tuition study at the GSB. All units must be taken at Stanford.",
