    "U07MAf5V-text": {
      "why": "\"To earn an MBA, a student entering the 2025-2026 academic year must be in good academic standing and fulfill the following list of requirements\". The 90 units, the 80 GSB units and the core are checked elsewhere. \"At least 70 must represent GSB units taken for a letter grade\" and \"At least 80 units must be completed for a letter grade (not on a Pass/Fail, +/U, or CR/NC basis; no more than 10 pass/fail units)\" are counted on the GSB's own grading basis, whose marks the audit reads as pass grades, so they are checked by hand. \"Achieve a cumulative grade point average (GPA) for all GSB courses, not less than 2.65.\" \"Complete an approved Global Experience by the start of the Winter Quarter of the second year of the program.\" \"Complete the Engaging with Differences Requirement (EDR) by the start of the Winter Quarter of the second year of the program.\" \"Enroll for six quarters, excluding summer, of full-tuition study at the GSB.\"",
